{"results": [{"id": "hp_doc_f0f37d82a2a5a1b9765cf937a9a0163ceea5035c7693f189a16651eadb516a34", "title": "Federico García Lorca", "text": "Federico del Sagrado Corazón de Jesús García Lorca, known as Federico García Lorca (] ; 5 June 1898 – 19 August 1936) was a Spanish poet, playwright, and theatre director.", "score": 27.9897}, {"id": "hp_doc_4aa9841f9a08858509705bfeabb12cff2ae116381d908798776e73c0798d4541", "title": "Concurso de Cante Jondo", "text": "El Concurso del Cante Jondo (Contest of the Deep Song) was a well-known celebration of the art of flamenco, its music, song, and dance, held in Granada, on Corpus Christi, the 13th and 14 June 1922. At conception the idea of composer Manuel de Falla, its organizating activities enjoyed early and strong support from poet Federico García Lorca. The two outdoor, evening events included amateur flamenco performers, as well as revered professionals.", "score": 15.37}, {"id": "hp_doc_750b7f66141c3c4afa53f5e7a3002379857fbe36718e4a83d6c97f78570fd099", "title": "Opera Rara", "text": "Opera Rara is a British non-profit recording company, founded in the early 1970s by American Patric Schmid and Englishman Don White to promote concerts of rare and/or forgotten operas by \"bel canto\" era composers such as Italian composers Gaetano Donizetti, Giovanni Pacini, Saverio Mercadante, and Federico Ricci, as well as French composers of the 1830s forward such as Giacomo Meyerbeer.", "score": 7.9388}], "remaining_searches": 1}
